urceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"PSA","canonicalOSIS":"Ps","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Ps"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Ps.111.1-117.2","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Ps.111.1-117.2","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Ps.111.1-10","r":"Ps.111.1-10","rawR":"Ps.111.1-10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.111.1-10","value":"Ps.111.1-10"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ps 111"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," This wisdom psalm contains many references to the works of the Lord that reveal his character. God is righteous, gracious, compassionate, faithful, just, trustworthy, upright, holy, and awe-inspiring (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.111.3","r":"Ps.111.3","rawR":"Ps.111.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.111.3","value":"Ps.111.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"111:3"},", ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.111.4","r":"Ps.111.4","rawR":"Ps.111.4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.111.4","value":"Ps.111.4"}],"t":"ref","v":"4"},", ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.111.7","r":"Ps.111.7","rawR":"Ps.111.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.111.7","value":"Ps.111.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"7"},", ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.111.8","r":"Ps.111.8","rawR":"Ps.111.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.111.8","value":"Ps.111.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"8"},", ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.111.9","r":"Ps.111.9","rawR":"Ps.111.9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.111.9","value":"Ps.111.9"}],"t":"ref","v":"9"},"). God’s character gives hope in the covenant relationship (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.111.5","r":"Ps.111.5","rawR":"Ps.111.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.111.5","value":"Ps.111.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"111:5"},"). He rescued Israel from Egypt (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.111.9","r":"Ps.111.9","rawR":"Ps.111.9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.111.9","value":"Ps.111.9"}],"t":"ref","v":"111:9"},"), gave them the land (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.111.6","r":"Ps.111.6","rawR":"Ps.111.6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.111.6","value":"Ps.111.6"}],"t":"ref","v":"111:6"},"), and provides for his people (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.111.5","r":"Ps.111.5","rawR":"Ps.111.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.111.5","value":"Ps.111.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"111:5"},"). However, God demands that the beneficiaries of this relationship also be people of righteousness and integrity."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Ps.111.1-10","refs":[{"book":"PSA","endChapter":111,"endVerse":10,"startChapter":111,"startVerse":1}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Ps.111.1-10","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"PSA","sourceChapterCoverage":[111],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"3754a1439e75a45fcaa015548e2ab4ae144d7d57bb25be05c761f12cb165a0c2","sourceItemName":"Ps.111.1-10","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":7177,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"PSA","canonicalOSIS":"Ps","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Ps"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Ps.111.1-10","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Ps.111.1-10","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Ps.111.1-5","r":"Ps.111.1-5","rawR":"Ps.111.1-5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.111.1-5","value":"Ps.111.1-5"}],"t":"ref","v":"111:1-5"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," The godly praise God and delight themselves in his great works. His mighty acts reflect his righteousness, grace, and compassion (see ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.116.5-7","r":"Ps.116.5-7","rawR":"Ps.116.5-7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.116.5-7","value":"Ps.116.5-7"}],"t":"ref","v":"116:5-7"},"). All who submit themselves to him experience his glory."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Ps.111.1-5","refs":[{"book":"PSA","endChapter":111,"endVerse":5,"startChapter":111,"startVerse":1}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Ps.111.1-5","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"PSA","sourceChapterCoverage":[111],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"362b3acbf720f3dfe5c89325dc7a5dcf6b8dd3efd0f95e292a29eeb7a7b57a7f","sourceItemName":"Ps.111.1-5","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":7178,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"PSA","canonicalOSIS":"Ps","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Ps"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Ps.111.1-5","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Ps.111.1-5","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Ps.111.5","r":"Ps.111.5","rawR":"Ps.111.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.111.5","value":"Ps.111.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"111:5"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," God takes care of his people’s needs, even providing ",{"c":["food"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"},". He ",{"c":["remembers his covenant"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," with Abraham (see ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.105.8-11","r":"Ps.105.8-11","rawR":"Ps.105.8-11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.105.8-11","value":"Ps.105.8-11"}],"t":"ref","v":"105:8-11"},")."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Ps.111.5","refs":[{"book":"PSA","endChapter":111,"endVerse":5,"startChapter":111,"startVerse":5}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Ps.111.5","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"PSA","sourceChapterCoverage":[111],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"76e5fed6d276918b6702e0f49115463760ee032cde85261f9721902e6c15df18","sourceItemName":"Ps.111.5","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":7179,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"PSA","canonicalOSIS":"Ps","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Ps"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Ps.111.5","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitl